course: dictionary
lesson: 9803
title: Showing off with swagger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To swagger is to walk or behave in a very proud, showy way, as if you think you are better than everyone else. You can tell a swagger from a normal walk because the person wants everyone to notice them.
explain: Read the context: «down the steps swaggers Toad in goggles, cap, gaiters, gauntlets and an enormous overcoat». Toad's huge, over-the-top outfit tells you he wants to be looked at. Swaggers is the verb: Toad is the one doing the proud, showy walking.
explain: The next sentence gives another clue: «His words fade when he sees their stern faces.» Toad's showy confidence drops away when people look serious, so the context shows swagger is about pride and show. Try swapping in "walks proudly and showily" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Swagger can also be a noun, meaning that proud, showy way itself, as in "he walked with swagger". In informal use, it can mean a confident style that others admire.
fact: Swagger is a verb (he swaggers, they swaggered) and a noun (swagger, which you cannot count).
fact: «Swagger» means to walk or behave in a very proud, showy way.
fact: Pirates and bullies often swagger in stories, to show that they think they are in charge.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad swaggers and boasts after his escapes.
fact: «Swag», the slang for cool style, comes from this word.
exercise: «down the steps swaggers Toad in goggles, cap, gaiters, gauntlets and an enormous overcoat» What does swaggers mean? | Runs away in fear | Creeps quietly and slowly | *Walks in a very proud, showy way | Falls down the steps
exercise: «His words fade when he sees their stern faces.» Find and copy one word that shows Toad's words stop. | goggles | *fade | overcoat | steps
exercise: Why do stories often show pirates and bullies swaggering? | To show they are cold and tired | To show they are scared and want to hide | *To show they think they are better than others | To show they are lost in the woods
test: Which word means walking or behaving in a very proud, showy way? | Gentle | *Swaggering | Shy | Sleepy
test: In slang, what does «swag» usually mean? | *Cool style | A heavy coat | A sad face | A long, slow walk
exam: Which sentence uses swagger as a noun? | They swaggered out of the room. | *He walked into the hall with real swagger. | She swaggers to the front of the class. | Toad swaggers down the steps.
